---
/**
 * The proof page: the honest evidence, generated rather than claimed.
 *
 * The scoreboard, the per-section bars and the full checklist all render from
 * `docs/roadmap.json`; the control map derives its statuses from the ledger
 * questions each control names, so this page cannot claim more than the ledger
 * does. The disclaimer sits at the top of the control map rather than the
 * bottom on purpose — a compliance section that leads with the good news and
 * buries the caveat is the exact genre this repository exists to argue against.
 *
 * `#generated-evidence` anchors the generated-data region (the homepage links
 * here); `#control-map` anchors the carried-over control map.
 */
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Scoreboard from '../components/Scoreboard.astro';
import SectionScoreboard from '../components/SectionScoreboard.astro';
import QuestionTable from '../components/QuestionTable.astro';
import StatusChip from '../components/StatusChip.astro';
import { inlineMarkdown } from '../components/inline';
import {
  frameworks,
  controlsInFramework,
  controlStatus,
  questionsFor,
  statusMeta,
  withBase,
  repoHref,
} from '../lib/roadmap';

const rows = frameworks.map((framework) => ({
  framework,
  controls: controlsInFramework(framework.id).map((control) => ({
    control,
    status: controlStatus(control),
    questions: questionsFor(control),
  })),
}));

const sectionEyebrow = 'font-mono text-xs tracking-widest text-ae-copper uppercase';
const cardRule = 'rounded-[2px] border border-ae-rule bg-ae-paper';
const btn =
  'inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-[2px] border border-ae-rule bg-ae-paper px-4 py-2.5 text-sm font-medium text-ae-ink transition-colors hover:border-ae-copper';
---

<Base
  title="Proof"
  description="The enterprise checklist and the control map, generated from the same roadmap file the documentation and CI use. Built answers, named gaps, no architecture theatre."
  active="proof"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-4 py-16 sm:px-6 sm:py-20 lg:px-8">
    <header>
      <p class={sectionEyebrow}>Proof</p>
      <h1
        class="mt-4 font-display text-4xl font-medium leading-tight tracking-tight text-balance text-ae-ink sm:text-5xl"
      >
        Built answers. Named gaps. No architecture theatre.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-lg leading-relaxed text-pretty text-muted">
        Every status is generated from the same roadmap file used by the documentation and CI. Follow
        any answer to its evidence — or to the gap it still names.
      </p>

      <div class="mt-10">
        <Scoreboard variant="hero" />
      </div>
    </header>

    {/* ==================== The generated evidence ==================== */}
    <section id="generated-evidence" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-24 border-t border-ae-rule pt-12">
      <p class={sectionEyebrow}>The generated evidence</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl font-medium tracking-tight text-balance text-ae-ink sm:text-4xl">
        Read the rows, not the total
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-4 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-pretty text-muted">
        One ratio across the whole checklist reports the project as uniformly half-finished, when in
        fact evidence is nearly done and assurance has barely started — and which of those a reader
        cares about depends entirely on why they came. The sections say which half.
      </p>

      <div class={cardRule + ' mt-8 p-6 sm:p-8'}>
        <SectionScoreboard />
      </div>

      <div class="mt-16">
        <QuestionTable />
      </div>

      <div class="mt-12 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a class={btn} href={withBase('/docs/questions/')}>The checklist, in prose</a>
        <a class={btn} href={withBase('/roadmap/')}>What is planned, and why <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    {/* ==================== The control map ==================== */}
    <section id="control-map" class="mt-20 scroll-mt-24 border-t border-ae-rule pt-12">
      <p class={sectionEyebrow}>Control map</p>
      <h2 class="mt-3 font-display text-3xl font-medium tracking-tight text-balance text-ae-ink sm:text-4xl">
        What an auditor asks, and where this actually stands
      </h2>

      {/* The disclaimer, first. */}
      <div class={cardRule + ' mt-10 p-6'}>
        <h3 class="font-mono text-xs tracking-widest text-ae-copper uppercase">What this is</h3>
        <div class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
          <p>
            This is an engineering document describing what the code does, written in the vocabulary an
            auditor uses. It is <strong class="font-semibold text-ae-ink">not</strong> an assertion of
            compliance, and it does not substitute for an audit.
          </p>
          <p>
            Roughly half of any real control is not in a repository at all: the policy, the training,
            the review cadence, the evidence that a human looked, and an auditor's judgement that all
            of it operated continuously over a six-to-twelve-month window. What follows covers the
            technical prerequisites — the part that is code, and can therefore be pointed at, tested,
            and shown not to have drifted.
          </p>
          <p>
            A control is scored by its <em>weakest</em> question, not its average. One open question
            means an auditor is going to ask, and rounding that up would misrepresent it.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      {
        rows.map(({ framework, controls }) => (
          <div id={`framework-${framework.id}`} class="mt-14 scroll-mt-24">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-x-4 gap-y-1">
              <h3 class="font-display text-2xl font-medium tracking-tight text-ae-ink">
                {framework.name}
              </h3>
              <p class="font-mono text-xs text-muted">{framework.revision}</p>
            </div>

            <ul class="mt-6 space-y-4">
              {controls.map(({ control, status, questions }) => (
                <li class="rounded-[2px] border border-ae-rule bg-ae-paper p-5">
                  <div class="flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-x-4 gap-y-2">
                    <h4 class="text-base font-semibold text-balance">
                      <span class="font-mono text-ae-copper">{control.id}</span>{' '}
                      <span class="text-ae-ink">{control.name}</span>
                    </h4>
                    <StatusChip status={status} />
                  </div>

                  <p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted italic">{control.asks}</p>

                  <p
                    class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted"
                    set:html={inlineMarkdown(control.note)}
                  />

                  <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 border-t border-ae-rule pt-4">
                    <span class="text-xs text-muted">Bearing on it:</span>
                    {questions.map((question) => (
                      <span
                        class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-[2px] border border-ae-rule bg-ae-paper-2 px-2 py-1 text-xs"
                        title={question.question}
                      >
                        <span aria-hidden="true">{statusMeta[question.status].icon}</span>
                        <span class="font-mono text-muted">{question.id}</span>
                        {question.proof ? (
                          <a
                            class="text-ae-copper underline-offset-4 hover:underline"
                            href={repoHref(question.proof)}
                          >
                            proof
                          </a>
                        ) : null}
                      </span>
                    ))}
                  </div>
                </li>
              ))}
            </ul>
          </div>
        ))
      }

      <div class={cardRule + ' mt-14 p-6 sm:p-8'}>
        <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-medium tracking-tight text-ae-ink">
          What writing this map found
        </h3>
        <div class="mt-4 space-y-4 text-sm leading-relaxed text-muted">
          <p>
            Mapping controls to questions is a search for holes, and it found two. <strong
              class="font-semibold text-ae-ink">Evidence of review</strong
            > had no question at all — logs existed, were complete, were protected, and nobody was
            reading them, which is the single most common finding in a real engagement. And <strong
              class="font-semibold text-ae-ink">cryptography appears in exactly one place</strong
            >: the SHA-256 over the audit chain. Encryption at rest, in transit and key management
            belong to the deployment, and this repository says nothing about them.
          </p>
          <p>
            Both are now rows on the ledger rather than absences nobody had named, which is the only
            useful thing a document like this does.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-6 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
          <a class={btn} href={withBase('/docs/compliance/')}>The same map, in the docs</a>
          <a class={btn} href={withBase('/docs/questions/')}>Every question, with its proof</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
